      <br />
      Joined: 24 Nov 2003<br />
      Posts: 41<br />
      Location: Cleveland, OH</span><br /></td></table></td>
    <td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="postbody">Don't get me wrong, I love the WarCraft universe and I was REALLY excited about WoW, but the timing was very bad on the release.  If EQ2 had been delayed, i would probably have bought WoW and skipped EQ2.
<br />

<br />
However, playing EQ for five years got me used to the world.  I know it's very different now, but I am intrigued by the story and how things will unfold.  I still miss the original game and the raiding.
<br />

<br />
I've paid for EQ2 and now have another family member playing, so I'm sticking to it.  Every time I think about switching to another game, I think about the time spent in EQ and how much enjoyment I got out of it.. I'm looking forward to that same enjoyment I felt working our way through Planes of Power and finally conquering the Plane of Time.. there's nothing quite like that.  I enjoyed the epic battles of EQ and the intense group dungeon crawling the most.. and some of that is evident in EQ2.
<br />

<br />
I'll never say "never", but for now....<br />_________________<br />- Me</span><span class="gensmall"><i></i></span></td>
        </tr>
